/-!
# Intrinsic characteristic kernels for the second Held model

Each of the 25 kernel intersections is generated by elements selected by an
intrinsic test: powers, the number of commuting involutions (including the
identity), or a centralizer of exponent two. Automorphisms preserve each test.
Checked positive words generate every kernel element from the selected elements;
the coordinate isomorphisms identify these with the actual published subgroups.

This discharges `CharacteristicChecks` without any census or radical premise.
It is the characteristic branch of the intermediate finite calculation for
Huppert--Blackburn III, XII.1.18(b), printed p.314, not the recognition theorem.
-/

namespace Theory.GroupTheory.HeldM22A10.SecondExclusion.ForceNormalizer.Candidates
